# Steps a ship needs besides the gate and the full suite, by the paths it changes since origin's
# main (SH-13): <extended regex over a changed path>, a tab, the step label, a tab, the exact
# command. tools/ship/commit-and-push requires the latest run of each matching step to have passed
# against the shipped tree from start to finish, as it does for the gate and the suite, and reads
# this file from origin as well as from the tree. Run each one as `tools/ship/timed <label>
# <command>`.
#
# A change to a control, its configuration, the build or the code the plants edit replays every
# control's planted bug (TS-5).
^(tools/checks/|tools/release/|test-fixtures/|config/|docker/Dockerfile$|compose\.yaml$|build\.gradle\.kts$|settings\.gradle\.kts$|gradle\.properties$|gradle/|[a-z-]*gradle\.lockfile$|(app|core)/|tools/templates/|templates/|tools/vendor-manifest\.tsv$)	plants	docker compose run --build --rm plants
# A change to the ship tool runs its own tests.
^(tools/ship/|\.githooks/|test/ship/|test/support/|docker/ship\.Dockerfile$|compose\.yaml$)	ship-tests	docker compose run --build --rm ship-tests
# A change to the app or its model runs every emulator scenario.
^(app/|core/src/main/|templates/|tools/templates/src/main/|test-fixtures/scenarios/|tools/checks/emulator$|tools/checks/tablet-avd$|tools/emulator$)	scenarios	tools/emulator test-fixtures/scenarios/all
# Every ship scans for known vulnerabilities (TC-10), so an advisory published since the last ship
# is found at the next one, whatever it changes. It needs the network, so it is not in the offline
# check.
.	vulns	docker compose run --rm vulns
